-- title:
--   A prime-to-p abelian-quotient family on the Néron object
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, a level datum $\Lambda$ of level $N_0$ at $p$ over $A$ (a structure map $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb Z_{(p)}$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb Z_{(p)}$ with a relative group law, and bijections $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0) = \operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ onto the generic points of $X$ and $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ at level $N_0$ over the residue field of $A$ onto the points of $X$ over the residue point) satisfying `IsJacobian` (abelian-scheme properties, commutativity, additivity and Galois-equivariance of both point dictionaries, compatibility of reduction mod the maximal ideal, and realisation of Hecke operators by endomorphisms), and a Néron object $O$ of level $N_0p$ over $\Lambda$. Then there is a single family, indexed by the naturals $m$ coprime to $p$, of additive maps
--   $$\mathrm{abq}_m \colon O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m \longrightarrow J_0(N_0) \times J_0(N_0),$$
--   where $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ is the subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ generated by the $m$-torsion classes $x$ whose associated generic point $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ extends to a point of $O.g$ over $\sigma_A$, such that: (1) every value of $\mathrm{abq}_m$ is killed by $m$; (2) for $m \mid m'$ with both coprime to $p$, $\mathrm{abq}_{m'}$ agrees with $\mathrm{abq}_m$ on points of $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ lying in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m'$; and (3) whenever $s$ is a point of $O.g$ over $\sigma_A$ with $(O.\mathrm{pts}\,x).1 = \mathrm{barPt}\,A$ followed by $s$, the reduction mod the maximal ideal of $A$ of the $i$-th component of $\mathrm{abq}_m(x)$, for $i = 0, 1$, is $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}$ applied to the image under `fibreMap` of `O.abqFibre i` of the restriction of $s$ to the residue point (the composite of $\mathrm{resPt}\,A$ with $s$).
--
--   This is the construction half of the abelian-quotient maps attached to the Néron model at $p$: on prime-to-$p$ torsion that extends over $A$, reduce the extension, apply the two abelian-quotient morphisms of the special fibre carried by the Néron object, and lift back along reduction, which is bijective on prime-to-$p$ torsion. It is used by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_abq_family_of_coprime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_abq_family_of_coprime), en route to the comparison of Galois representations at level $N_0p$ and level $N_0$ in the level-lowering argument.
